1
00:03:30,967 --> 00:03:36,967
The Machines Will Rise.

2
00:07:01,935 --> 00:07:07,935
Terminator 3: Rise of the Machines is a action, thriller,
science fiction film directed by Jonathan Mostow.

3
00:10:32,903 --> 00:10:38,903
It's been 10 years since John Connor saved Earth from Judgment Day, and he's now
living under the radar, steering clear of using anything Skynet can trace.

4
00:14:03,870 --> 00:14:09,870
That is, until he encounters T-X, a robotic assassin
ordered to finish what T-1000 started.

5
00:17:34,838 --> 00:17:40,838
Good thing Connor's former nemesis, the Terminator, is back to
aid the now-adult Connor … just like he promised.

6
00:21:05,806 --> 00:21:11,806
The Terminator, played by Arnold Schwarzenegger.

7
00:24:36,774 --> 00:24:42,774
John Connor, played by Nick Stahl.

8
00:28:07,741 --> 00:28:13,741
Kate Brewster, played by Claire Danes.

9
00:31:38,709 --> 00:31:44,709
T-X, played by Kristanna Loken.

10
00:35:09,677 --> 00:35:15,677
Dr. Peter Silberman, played by Earl Boen.

11
00:38:40,645 --> 00:38:46,645
Robert Brewster, played by David Andrews.

12
00:42:11,612 --> 00:42:17,612
Terminator 3: Rise of the Machines is a 2003 science fiction action film, the third installment
in the Terminator franchise and a sequel to Terminator 2: Judgment Day (1991).

13
00:45:42,580 --> 00:45:48,580
It was directed by Jonathan Mostow and stars Arnold
Schwarzenegger, Nick Stahl, Claire Danes, and Kristanna Loken.

14
00:49:13,548 --> 00:49:19,548
In its plot, the malevolent artificial intelligence Skynet sends a T-X (Loken)—a highly advanced Terminator—back in time to ensure the
rise of machines by killing top members of the future human resistance as John Connor's (Stahl) location is unknown.

15
00:52:44,516 --> 00:52:50,516
The resistance sends back a reprogrammed T-850 (Schwarzenegger) to
protect John and his future wife, Kate Brewster (Danes).

16
00:56:15,483 --> 00:56:21,483
While Terminator creator James Cameron was interested in directing the third
film, he ultimately had no involvement with Terminator 3.

17
00:59:46,451 --> 00:59:52,451
Vajna and Mario Kassar, who had produced Terminator 2: Judgment Day through their company Carolco Pictures, obtained the
rights for the franchise through both Carolco's liquidation auction and negotiations with producer Gale Ann Hurd.

18
01:03:17,419 --> 01:03:23,419
In 1999, Tedi Sarafian was hired to write the first draft of the script.

19
01:06:48,387 --> 01:06:54,387
Mostow joined the project as director in 2001, and he brought on John
Brancato and Michael Ferris to rewrite Sarafian's script.

20
01:10:19,354 --> 01:10:25,354
The $187 million budget included a $5 million salary for Mostow
and a record $30 million salary for Schwarzenegger.

21
01:13:50,322 --> 01:13:56,322
Filming took place in California from April to September 2002.

22
01:17:21,290 --> 01:17:27,290
Industrial Light & Magic and Stan Winston created the special
effects, as they did for the previous film.

23
01:20:52,258 --> 01:20:58,258
Terminator 3: Rise of the Machines premiered at the Mann Village Theater in Westwood, Los
Angeles, on June 30, 2003, and was released on July 2, 2003, by Warner Bros.

24
01:24:23,225 --> 01:24:29,225
Pictures in North America.

25
01:27:54,193 --> 01:28:00,193
The film was rolled out overseas throughout the next few months, with Columbia
Pictures overseeing the bulk of the international distribution.

26
01:31:25,161 --> 01:31:31,161
It received generally positive reviews and earned $433.4 million worldwide,
finishing its theatrical run as the seventh-highest-grossing film of 2003.

27
01:34:56,129 --> 01:35:02,129
The film was also used to mark Schwarzenegger's formal entry into politics, having
been speculated to be a vehicle for his 2003 gubernatorial run.

28
01:38:27,096 --> 01:38:33,096
A sequel, Terminator Salvation, was released in 2009.

29
01:41:58,064 --> 01:42:04,064
The film explores themes of man vs machine, artificial intelligence
(a.i.), saving the world, leather jacket, cyborg.

30
01:45:29,032 --> 01:45:35,032
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
